   306	
   307	### 7.3 Pre-registered reachability in the public-proxy domain
   308	
   309	G0, G1.1, G1.2, G5, and G6.2 are `NOT_MEASURABLE_IN_DOMAIN`. Therefore rules 3
   310	and 4 **cannot be satisfied** in the public-proxy domain under v1. The
   311	reachable results are:
   312	
   313	- **NOT FEASIBLE (AI-adjudicated, public-proxy domain; frame-scoped)** through
   314	  rule 2;
   315	- **INSUFFICIENT INFORMATION (AI-adjudicated, public-proxy domain)** through
   316	  rule 5;
   317	- process status **UNADJUDICATED** through rule 1.
   318	
   319	This outcome space is stated before any evidence is inspected. Because the
   320	supply bound covers the whole frame (section 6.4) and requires the R3
   321	certificate (section 7.4), NOT FEASIBLE is expected to be reachable only if
   322	the frame is small and fully enumerated; the most likely v1 outcome is
   323	INSUFFICIENT INFORMATION. That expectation is recorded here so it cannot be
   324	presented later as a finding. The public-proxy
   325	substitution cannot produce a positive classification; reaching one requires a
   326	later rules version that adds an evidence source able to measure G0, G1, G5,
   327	and G6.2 as originally defined.
   328	
   329	### 7.4 Method-independent necessary cluster count (supply route)
   330	
   331	**Setting.** Source clusters are independent and identically distributed draws
   332	of a complete cluster observation `X` (all arms, all slots, all outcomes, with
   333	arbitrary within-cluster and cross-arm dependence). The safety component G3.1
   334	of either branch concerns `D = mean over the cluster's slots of (subject
   335	escape) - mean of (comparator escape)`, with `-1 <= D <= 1`, and the null
   336	`E[D] >= +0.01`. The test is level 0.025 (branch alpha) and must be valid over
   337	every admissible joint distribution, because the cluster is the independent
   338	unit (Draft v3 section 5.1; section 4.2).
   339	
   340	**Bound.** Let `P1` be any cluster distribution with `E[D] = -0.01` (the
   341	registered most-favorable alternative, section 4.3). Let `Q` be a cluster
   342	distribution with `D = +1` almost surely (every subject slot is a serious
   343	escape and no comparator slot is; this is coherent because a serious escape
   344	only requires an accepted, incorrect artifact). Define
   345	`P0 = (1 - eps) P1 + eps Q` with `eps = 0.02 / 1.01`, so
   346	`E_P0[D] = (1 - eps)(-0.01) + eps = +0.01`: `P0` is on the null boundary and
   347	the branch claim is false under it. For n clusters, the product measure
   348	satisfies `P0^n >= (1 - eps)^n P1^n` on every event, so for any test `phi`,
   349	`E_P1[phi] <= E_P0[phi] / (1 - eps)^n <= 0.025 / (1 - eps)^n`. Power 0.80 at
   350	`P1` therefore requires `(1 - eps)^n <= 0.025 / 0.80`, that is
   351	
   352	`N_MIN = ceil( ln(0.025 / 0.80) / ln(1 - 0.02/1.01) ) = 174`.
   353	
   354	The bound holds uniformly over every `P1` with mean difference -1 pp, every
   355	base rate, every within-cluster dependence, every repetition count, and every
   356	ascertainment method. It needs no grid, no simulation, and no nuisance range.
   357	The frozen calculator [r1-safety-nmin.py](r1-safety-nmin.py) evaluates this
   358	closed form. (A round-2 reviewer proposed this argument after showing that the
   359	earlier marginal Neyman-Pearson argument was invalid for paired outcomes.)
   360	
   361	**Admissibility certificate.** The bound uses the null point `P0`, which
   362	mixes in `Q`. It applies only if `Q` is admissible under the frozen design:
   363	every eligible cluster type can, under the design's model, have a serious
   364	escape in every subject slot and none in any comparator slot. A design that
   365	uses known structural constraints in inference (for example a stratum whose
   366	escape probability is fixed at zero or at a known value, or known stratum
   367	proportions used to bound escape rates) can make `Q` inadmissible, and then a
   368	valid test may need fewer clusters. R3 must therefore record, before R2B′
   369	inspects data, either (a) a certificate that the confirmatory analysis uses no
   370	such constraint (the model for each cluster's escape outcomes is
   371	unrestricted, apart from the coherence `e <= a - k` that `Q` satisfies), or
   372	(b) the constraints it does use. Under (b), or if no certificate is recorded,
   373	the supply route is **disabled** and G3.1 cannot be `SIZED_INFEASIBLE`.
   374	
   375	**Rule:** G3.1 is `SIZED_INFEASIBLE` (in both branches) if and only if the
   376	R3 certificate (a) is recorded, `F_high` is finite, and `F_high < N_MIN`, that
   377	is, `H_high <= 130` (`floor(130 / 0.75) = 173`; `floor(131 / 0.75) = 174`).
   378	
   379	**Scope.** The bound does not depend on how acceptance or escapes are
   380	ascertained, on reviewer type, or on cost. It holds for the original endpoint.
   381	What it scopes is the **supply**: it shows that a study drawing its final pool
   382	from the frozen frame cannot reach 80% power for the +1 pp safety gate under
   383	the registered most-favorable alternative, for any valid test. It does not show
   384	that an adopter-domain study could not. Pilot reservations are taken as zero
   385	and authored clusters at their 25% cap, both favorable to feasibility. A larger
   386	true safety advantage than -1 pp would lower `N_MIN`; -1 pp is the registered
   387	most-favorable alternative, fixed before inspection, and cannot be changed
   388	after inspection (section 10).
   389	
   390	### 7.5 Countersignature of a classification
   391	
   392	A classification is formal only when R5 records: the rules version and file
   393	hashes; the R2B/R4 output hashes; a Codex adversarial round under
   394	[r1-methods-governance.md](r1-methods-governance.md) stating "no blocking
   395	objections" against the R5 artifact SHA; and the maintainer's merge. The
   396	maintainer action (STOP, DEFER, ALLOW A SEPARATE AUTHORIZATION REQUEST) is a
   397	separate field.
   398	
   399	### 7.6 Non-statistical route checklists and state assignment
   400	
   401	| Gate | Checklist items |
   402	|---|---|
   403	| G4 | (a) frozen mechanism suite with negative controls covering the supported construct/property matrix; (b) isolated acceptance boundary with access separation (not the legacy `run-pair.sh` seam); (c) bypass probes for every protected requirement; (d) **recorded results** of (a)-(c) showing zero confirmed false-established properties and zero accepted unauthorized bypasses, and no open unexcluded false-established finding in the supported matrix (#1311) |
   404	| G6.1 | (a) export pipeline producing runnable C# for every supported construct; (b) behavioral comparison against the approved requirements with **recorded passing results** for every supported construct; (c) documented lost static guarantees and remaining runtime checks |
   405	
   406	An item is **absent** when no artifact for it exists. It is **unresolved**
   407	when an artifact exists but any of these holds: it does not cover the whole
   408	supported matrix; any result is invalid, indeterminate, unmeasurable, or not
   409	yet validity-checked; a finding's confirmation is pending; or any reviewer
   410	(Codex, Copilot, or the maintainer) has recorded an unresolved objection. The
   411	status depends on the evidence, not on whether a reviewer has noticed it.
   412	Assign exactly one state by the first matching step:
   413	
   414	1. `ROUTE_BLOCKED` if any recorded result violates the gate metric (a
   415	   confirmed false-established property, an accepted unauthorized bypass, or a
   416	   failed behavioral comparison), whatever the state of other items.
   417	2. `ROUTE_UNRESOLVED` if any item is unresolved.
   418	3. `ROUTE_MISSING` if any item is absent.
   419	4. `ROUTE_ESTABLISHED` if every item is present, complete, validity-checked,
   420	   undisputed, and passing against the gate metric.
   421	5. Otherwise `ROUTE_UNRESOLVED`. This step makes the assignment exhaustive.
   422	
   423	### 7.7 Interpretation limits
   424	
   425	- NOT FEASIBLE means: a three-arm study drawing its final pool from the frozen
   426	  public-proxy frame cannot reach 80% power for the +1 pp safety gate under the
   427	  most-favorable registered alternative, for any valid test. It does not
   428	  establish infeasibility for an adopter-domain study, for a different frame,
   429	  universal impossibility, or absence of value.
   430	- INSUFFICIENT INFORMATION is a stopped inquiry, not evidence of no demand or
